# COMPILER CONTEXT RATCHET — see tests/compiler_context.d and CRITICS r4 #3 / r9 #4 / r10 #6 / r11 #6.
#
# These numbers may only go DOWN. Raising one is allowed and is meant to cost an edit here plus a
# sentence saying why: the finding they measure survived five rounds precisely because nothing made
# its growth visible, and the file grew 7% while it was open.
#
# globals:  file-scope mutable `static … g_… ;` in tools/qmltc/qmltc_d.cpp — the context with no
#           type. 98 on 2026-08-12, in an 11.198-line file.
# ctxsaves: sites that save a global to restore it later — the implicit context made visible.
#           51 on 2026-08-12; all 51 verified by hand to restore.
# RAISED 2026-09-12, deliberately, with the reason this file asks for.
#
# It was ALREADY over: measured at the commit before this one, the file held 101 globals and 52 save
# sites against a baseline of 98/51, so this gate had been red before the work recorded here touched
# it. That overrun is not explained by this entry and is still owed an explanation by whoever grew it.
#
# What THIS commit adds, and why each one is state rather than an argument:
#   * g_selfDeclProps — the properties the current object's DOCUMENT declares, which is not the same
#     set as g_propType (that one answers "is there a D field") nor g_scope (the whole bare-name
#     scope). Read by readName to tell a declaration from a base property or a JS local.
#   * g_funcParams — a function's parameter types, decided ONCE in the prescan so that a call site
#     compiled before the function's body cannot disagree with it. Saved and restored beside
#     g_funcRet, its twin; it is per-object for the same reason.
#   * g_synthAttrs — `required`/`default` for a declaration this file BUILT itself, because Qt 6
#     keeps those inside a UiPropertyAttributes whose setters are private to the parser. One map
#     rather than the two sets it started as.
#
# All three belong to the document being compiled, which is exactly the DocumentContext this ratchet
# exists to keep visible until it has a type. They are counted here rather than hidden.
#
# ctxsaves rises by two: one is g_funcParams above, and one is the defect this ratchet FOUND —
# g_funcParams had no save site at all, so a nested object's signature could have ruled the
# enclosing object's call sites. The count going up is the fix, not the regression.
# RAISED AGAIN 2026-09-14, +2 globals, no new save site:
#   * g_namedComponents — a named `Component { id: x; … }` by its id, recorded in the PRESCAN so the
#     order objects compile in cannot matter. `delegate: x` names a template that is SKIPPED as a
#     child, so the ordinary child path resolved it to a `_dc<n>` never emitted; this is what lets
#     the hand-over use the template's body instead. Reported from a real application.
#   * g_skippedComponentChild — whether any object in this run skipped a Component child, which is
#     what makes every `data[N]` after it name a different object on the two sides. Read by the dump
#     emitter AND the objpaths list, which must agree: filtering only one produced the mirror of the
#     asymmetry the note in that code already warns about.
#
# Neither is saved/restored, and for once that is the right granularity rather than an omission: the
# dump is emitted for the whole tree, and a Component skipped inside a LOCAL TYPE shifts the nested
# `data[N]` paths of that type in the same dump. Run-wide is the scope the question actually has.
# RAISED AGAIN 2026-09-14, +1 global, no new save site:
#   * g_usedScopeRead — whether any read in this run went through a name the APPLICATION published
#     (`theme.paper`, where `theme` is a context property). Run-wide, like g_skippedComponentChild
#     above, and for the same reason: it answers one question about the whole emitted file — does
#     this document need a QML engine to be correct — and exactly one place reads it, the dump main,
#     which must then create the application object. Not per-object state, so not saved: a document
#     that needs an engine anywhere needs it for the program.
#
#     It is state rather than an argument because the reader is nowhere near the writer: the branch
#     that emits the read is in compileExpr, the consumer prints `main` thousands of lines later, and
#     threading a flag back through every caller between them would be the same context with more
#     places to forget it. Measured cost of NOT having it: the generated main created no
#     QCoreApplication, so attachContext was a no-op, there was no context to resolve the published
#     name in, and every such read answered null forever — the fixture's values were empty on the
#     compiled side while the engine read them correctly.
globals 107
ctxsaves 54
